{"term":"sore","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:0d4fa2e27ece0206e5","definition":"Causing pain or discomfort; painfully sensitive.","example":"Her feet were sore from walking so far.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["aching","smarting","achesome","aching","achy","raw","hurt","hurty","griefful","pained","painfilled","painful","smartful","smarting","sore","suffering","tender","tormented"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sore#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7edb23d67546a558b5","definition":"Sensitive; tender; easily pained, grieved, or vexed; very susceptible of irritation.","example":"Malice and hatred are very fretting and vexatious, and apt to make our minds sore and uneasy.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["delicate","fragile","tetchy","touchy"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sore#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8e18370d3db8f51eab","definition":"Dire; distressing.","example":"The school was in sore need of textbooks, theirs having been ruined in the flood.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sore#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1801ee98deed98c9d1","definition":"Feeling animosity towards someone; annoyed or angered.","example":"Joe was sore at Bob for beating him at checkers.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["irked","ratty","annoyed","angry","aggravated","agitated","bothered","exasperated","frustrated","irritable","irritated","irked","peeved","pestered","pissy","ratty","shitty","sore","tired","vexed",